UID:767eae534305f483@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260817T185529Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260817
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Statement of Attorney General Aaron M. Frey P
 rompted by the Shadow Hearing on the Use of Deadly Force by ICE in the dea
 th of Johan Sebastián Durán Guerrero
DESCRIPTION:FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE\nContact: Danna Hayes\,\nDanna.hayes@mai
 ne.gov\nStatement of Attorney General Aaron M. Frey Prompted by the Shadow
  Hearing on the Use of Deadly Force by ICE in the death of Johan Sebastiá
 n Durán Guerrero\nAUGUSTA –\nThe Office of the Maine Attorney General c
 ontinues to actively investigate the shooting death of Mr. Johan Sebastiá
 n Durán Guerrero by a federal Enforcement Removal Operations Officer in B
 iddeford on July 13\, 2026.\nUnder Maine Law\, the Attorney General’s Of
 fice has exclusive responsibility both for any criminal investigation of a
  homicide and for the use of deadly force by law enforcement acting in an 
 official capacity. In cooperation with relevant local\, state and federal 
 agencies\, this office has been collecting\, processing\, and analyzing ev
 idence to determine whether Maine law authorizes legal action to address t
 he conduct.\nOnce the investigation is complete and the Attorney General h
 as determined whether available evidence supports any action under Maine l
 aw\, the entire file will be provided to the Maine Deadly Force Review Pan
 el\, as contemplated by 5 M.R.S § 200-K\, for review and recommendations 
 in effort to minimize and\, to the greatest extent possible\, prevent the 
 use of deadly force.\nAs a general matter\, neither the Office of the Main
 e Attorney General nor the Maine Deadly Force Review Panel may exercise ju
 risdiction over the practices of the Department of Homeland Security\, and
  it will be the responsibility of either the federal administration or Con
 gress to address any questions raised by such review.\nFinally\, the Offic
 e of the Maine Attorney General is keenly aware of the public interest in 
 this case and is committed to a thorough\, impartial investigation that en
 sures meaningful transparency and public confidence. While completeness an
 d transparency are objectives of equal importance\, protecting the integri
 ty of the investigation takes priority while evidence is still being gathe
 red. This Office is regularly assessing whether s\nhttps://www.maine.gov/a
 g/news-and-library/press-releases/statement-attorney-general-aaron-m-frey-
 prompted-shadow-hearing-use
URL:https://www.maine.gov/ag/news-and-library/press-releases/statement-att
 orney-general-aaron-m-frey-prompted-shadow-hearing-use
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:9a357b4f58fdb4a3@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260817T130341Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260805
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Cancellation of Certificate of Title for Tiny
  Home and Manufactured Home
DESCRIPTION:Important Information Regarding Cancellation of Certificate of
  Title:\nPursuant to\nTitle 29-A\, section §669\n\, beginning on July 29\
 , 2026\, residents of the state of Maine are able to request cancellation 
 of their Certificate of Title for Tiny Home or Manufactured Home for purpo
 ses of obtaining residential real property.\nWhen a Tiny Home or Manufactu
 red Home is\npermanently affixed to land that you own\, or land where you 
 have permission from the land owner via a signed sworn statement\n\, you m
 ay request to cancel the Certificate of Title. Once the Certificate of Tit
 le is cancelled\, the home becomes part of the residential real property i
 nstead of being treated as personal property. Under Maine law\, this proce
 ss is handled through the county Registry of Deeds and the Maine Secretary
  of State Bureau of Motor Vehicles.\nHow to Cancel your Certificate of Tit
 tle for Tiny Home or Manufactured Home\nBefore requesting cancellation of 
 the title\, make sure:\nYou own the Tiny Home or Manufactured Home\nand\nt
 he land where it is located\;\nand/or\nThe individual that owns the proper
 ty has given a sworn signed statement of authorization.\nThe home has been
 \npermanently affixed\nto the property in accordance with Maine law.\nAny 
 existing liens have been released or the lienholder has agreed to release 
 the lien upon cancellation of the title.\nThis process is not for double-w
 ide mobile homes/trailers\n1. Gather the required documentation\nYou will 
 need to obtain the following documents before submitting your request:\nTh
 e Original Certificate of Title\nA description of the home\, including\;\n
 Model Year\nManufacturer {make}\nWidth\nLength\nIdentification Number/Seri
 al Number\nLien Release Documentation\,\nif applicable\nThe legal descript
 ion of the real property\nA sworn statement confirming:\nYou own both the 
 land\, and the Tiny Home or Manufactured Home\, or a sworn statement from 
 the property land owner\nThe home is permanently affixed to the property/g
 round\nIf you are unable to locate your current Certificate of T\nhttps://
 www.maine.gov/sos/bmv/vehicles/titles/tiny-and-manufactured-homes-conversi
 on-to-real-property
URL:https://www.maine.gov/sos/bmv/vehicles/titles/tiny-and-manufactured-ho
 mes-conversion-to-real-property
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
