DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260813
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Section 50\, Intermediate Care Facilities for
  Individuals with Intellectual Disabilities (ICF/IID): New Fiscal Year (FY
 ) 27 and REVISED FY26 Rates & Letters\, CR 141649\, 141868
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Section 50\, Intermediate Care Facilities for Individua
 ls with Intellectual Disabilities (ICF/IID): New Fiscal Year (FY) 27 and R
 EVISED FY26 Rates & Letters\, CR 141649\, 141868\nSection 50\, Intermediat
 e Care Facilities for Individuals with Intellectual Disabilities (ICF/IID)
 : New Fiscal Year (FY) 27 and REVISED FY26 Rates & Letters\, CR 141649\, 1
 41868\nAug 13\, 2026\nNew FY27 and revised FY26 rate letters are available
  on the secure part of the Health PAS Online Portal. You can view them by 
 logging into your Trading Partner Account and following this pathway: File
  Exchange > Reports > Rate Setting Letters.\nRevised FY26 Rate Letters\nTh
 e Department recently identified and corrected an error in the FY26 (July 
 1\, 2025 – June 30\, 2026) rate calculations for ICF/IIDs. This error re
 sulted in overinflation of the variable rate.\nProviders do not need to ad
 just FY26 claims.\nIf we identify overpayments or\nunderpayments during th
 e audit review\, providers will be notified pursuant to MaineCare Benefits
  Manual\, Chapter III\, Section 50\, Principle 7076.\nFY27 Adjustment Bill
 ing Guidance for Dates of Service July 1\, through July 30\, 2026\nProvide
 rs are responsible for adjusting all affected claims. Per policy and to av
 oid timely filing denials\, you must submit adjustments within 120 days of
  the most recent claim payment date.  For additional billing guidance whe
 n adjusting or reversing claims\, please see the\nHow to Adjust Claims for
  Retro Rate Increases (PDF) document.\nIf you have questions about accessi
 ng the letters\, please contact Provider Services at: 1-866-690-5585.\nFo
 r questions about the content of the letters\, please contact Rate Setting
  directly by contacting the representative listed on the letters.\nhttps:/
 /www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/section-50-intermedia
 te-care-facilities-individuals-intellectual-disabilities-icfiid-new
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/section-50
 -intermediate-care-facilities-individuals-intellectual-disabilities-icfiid
 -new
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a6d5de8d8880d1c3@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260814T024310Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260813
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Pharmacy Prior Authorization and Claims Denia
 ls: Enroll to Avoid Denials
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Pharmacy Prior Authorization and Claims Denials: Enroll
  to Avoid Denials\nPharmacy Prior Authorization and Claims Denials: Enroll
  to Avoid Denials\nAug 13\, 2026\nAs\npreviously communicated\n\, billing 
 providers must include the National Provider Identifier (NPI) of an enroll
 ed MaineCare practitioner who is ordering\, prescribing\, or referring on 
 claims submitted to MaineCare. This is a federal requirement. In the next 
 few months\, MaineCare will begin to\ndeny pharmacy PAs\nfor prescriptions
  written by providers who are not enrolled with MaineCare\, and will subse
 quently begin to\ndeny Point of Sale pharmacy claims\nthat do not have the
  NPI of an enrolled prescriber on the claim.\nThis requirement is for:\nAl
 l prescription claims\, including Point of Sale claims\nClinical laborator
 ies for ordered tests\nImaging centers for ordered imaging procedures\nDur
 able Medical Equipment\, Prosthetics\, Orthotics and Supplies (DMEPOS)\nEn
 roll with MaineCare today!\nMake sure your patients can continue to get th
 eir medications covered by ensuring any unenrolled prescribing providers c
 omplete an online application through the\nHealth PAS Online Portal\n. Pr
 oviders that do not plan to seek MaineCare reimbursement may continue pres
 cribing medications to MaineCare members by enrolling specifically as a No
 n-Billing\, Ordering\, Prescribing or Referring (NOPR) provider\, which is
  a shorter process. The NOPR enrollment is faster and requires less docume
 ntation than a regular MaineCare enrollment – and is free to complete.\n
 We encourage unenrolled prescribers to start by visiting the\nProvider Enr
 ollment & Revalidation webpage\nfor helpful resources to guide you through
  the enrollment process.\nContact us for assistance.\nFor assistance with 
 the enrollment process\, please contact Provider Services by\nemail\nor ca
 ll 1-866-690-5585\, Option 2. TTY users dial 711.\nhttps://www.maine.gov/d
 hhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/pharmacy-prior-authorization-and-clai
 ms-denials-enroll-avoid-denials-2026-08-13
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/pharmacy-p
 rior-authorization-and-claims-denials-enroll-avoid-denials-2026-08-13
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
