UID:0d6a3607f0397fa6@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260810T191354Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260803
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Standing Order: Standing Order on Servicememb
 ers or Spouses of Servicemembers Seeking Admission to the Maine Bar
DESCRIPTION:STATE OF MAINE \nSUPREME JUDICIAL COURT \nSTANDING ORDER ON SE
 RVICEMEMBERS OR SPOUSES OF SERVICEMEMBERS \nSEEKING ADMISSION TO THE MAINE
  BAR \n \nEffective August 3\, 2026 \nAttorneys who are servicemembers or 
 spouses of servicemembers \nassigned to Maine and who wish to be licensed 
 in Maine while they or their \nspouses are stationed here may seek waiver 
 of strict compliance with the \nduration of practice requirement of the ru
 le g overning admission by motion \nwithout examination\, Maine Bar Admiss
 ion Rule 11A(a)(2).  The Maine \nSupreme Judicial Court\, the Maine Board 
 of Overseers of the Bar\, and the Maine \nBoard of Bar Examiners are commi
 tted to working with these applicants to \naccommodate their unique circum
 stances and to expedite the bar application \nprocess to the extent possib
 le when they or their spouses’ service brings them \nto Maine. \nThe Cou
 rt will consider requests for waiver on a case -by-case basis\, \ndependin
 g on the individual circumstances of the applicant.   Servicemembers \nand
  spouses of servicemembers are encouraged to contact the Maine Supreme \nJ
 udicial Court Clerk’s Office at (207)822-4146 for more information about
  the \nwaiver process. Servicemembers and spouses of servicemembers assign
 ed to \nMaine who wish to take the Maine bar examination but have missed a
  deadline \nto apply for the exam\, should also contact the Maine Board of
  Bar Examiners at \n(207)623-2464 or execdir@mainebarexaminers.org for ass
 istance. \nPromulgation Date: 8/3/2026 FOR THE COURT: \n \n \n   /s/      
 \nVALERIE STANFILL \nChief Justice \n \nAndrew M. Mead \nCatherine R. Conn
 ors \nRick E. Lawrence \nWayne R. Douglas \nJulia M. Lipez \nChristopher C
 . Taub\nhttps://www.courts.maine.gov/adminorders/so-service-members.pdf
URL:https://www.courts.maine.gov/adminorders/so-service-members.pdf
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:8a200ca55b166c26@role-estate-probate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260810T134115Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260810
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Upcoming Pause in Configuration Changes
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Upcoming Pause in Configuration Changes\nUpcoming Pause
  in Configuration Changes\nAug 10\, 2026\nAs\npreviously communicated\n\, 
 the Office of MaineCare Services is launching an upgraded MIHMS\, our clai
 ms processing system\, in October 2026. To support system readiness activi
 ties\, MaineCare is temporarily pausing the implementation of configuratio
 n changes from the end of August to the end of October.\nCoding and NDC Re
 quests\nContinue submitting coding requests to\nOMS.referencefile@maine.go
 v\nand NDC/J-Code Requests to\nMaineCareNDCrequest.DHHS@maine.gov\n. Reque
 sts submitted by August 19\, 2026\, if approved\, will be implemented no l
 ater than the last synchronization on August 25\, 2026. Continue to submit
  these requests as usual after these dates. MaineCare will review and docu
 ment change requests beginning at the end of October.\nRate Change Request
 s\nContinue submitting rate change requests as usual to\nMIHMSRateRqst.DHH
 S@maine.gov\nthroughout this period. MaineCare will review and document ch
 ange requests as appropriate for implementation beginning at the end of Oc
 tober.\nClaims and Billing Inquiries\nContinue directing claims and billin
 g inquiries to Provider Services at 1-866-690-5585. We will continue revie
 wing claim denials to determine if a configuration change is needed. Maine
 Care will review and document change requests as appropriate for implement
 ation before the configuration pause or beginning at the end of October.\n
 We appreciate your continued cooperation during this transition. If you ha
 ve questions about the configuration pause or the status of a request\, pl
 ease contact\nyou\nr\nProvider Relations Specialist\n.\nhttps://www.maine.
 gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/upcoming-pause-configuration-cha
 nges-2026-08-04-0
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/upcoming-p
 ause-configuration-changes-2026-08-04-0
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
